//! View model of `templates/%%DIR%%/%%NAME%%.html`, a page generated by
//! `forge generate view %%DIR%%/%%NAME%%`. A handler renders it with
//! `forge::web::html(&%%TYPE%% { layout: site.layout(&request), title, content })`.

use askama::Template;

use super::Layout;

/// `templates/%%DIR%%/%%NAME%%.html`: fills the `title` and `content` blocks
/// of `templates/layouts/application.html`; every value is HTML-escaped.
#[derive(Template)]
#[template(path = "%%DIR%%/%%NAME%%.html")]
pub struct %%TYPE%%<'a> {
    pub layout: Layout<'a>,
    pub title: &'a str,
    pub content: &'a str,
}
